# P0.1 — this is not yet “the AI writes itself”

`ReincarnationAuthor` is currently a deterministic hand-written compiler:

```python
if opponent slow:
    boost = .7

elif opponent low-spin:
    tangential = .6

elif opponent holds center:
    orbit

...
```

and then always emits essentially the same four-state architecture:

```text
OBSERVE
PRESSURE
ORBIT
RECOVER
```

It does **not currently consume**:

```text
AgentState
career memory
opponent model
previous reincarnation
post-match reflection
Daimon
human coaching
strategic hypotheses
reincarnation lineage
```

despite those being the conceptual reason reincarnation exists.

So this is currently:

```text
mechanical report
→ deterministic heuristic compiler
→ RBZ-RC-1
```

not yet:

```text
persistent AI intelligence
→ reasons about opponent/history
→ authors novel RBZ-RC-1 architecture
```

That's perfectly acceptable for MVP, but the docs should call it:

> **reference reincarnation author / deterministic MVP author**

rather than implying the persistent AI is already self-compiling.

The next author interface should look more like:

```text
ReincarnationContext
├ agent_snapshot
├ mechanical_report
├ opponent_model
├ public opponent history
├ own reincarnation lineage
├ previous reflections
├ Daimon advice
├ human coaching events
├ current body
├ abilities
├ ruleset
└ compute budget
```

Then:

```python
author.reincarnate(context) -> ReincarnationManifest
```

The current author becomes:

```text
BaselineReincarnationAuthor
```

and later:

```text
LLMReincarnationAuthor
EvolutionaryReincarnationAuthor
HybridReincarnationAuthor
```

This is the defining mechanic, so this abstraction matters.

