# 3. Challenge nonce semantics need cleaning up

Battle-level reincarnation commitment uses:

```python
nonce = f"{base_seed}|{spec_a.id}|{spec_b.id}"
```

while the engine independently uses:

```python
nonce = f"{match_id}|{seed}|{ENGINE_VERSION}"
```

for generic policy commitments.

So there are currently two commitment protocols.

That's unnecessary and potentially confusing.

I'd have exactly one:

```text
MatchChallenge
├ match_id
├ ruleset_version
├ arena_version
├ body versions
└ challenge_nonce
```

Agents submit:

```text
reincarnation_commitment
```

then the match begins.

Afterward:

```text
manifest reveal
→ recompute hash
→ verify
```

One protocol. One audit trail.

