# P0.5 — `mechanical_version` is recorded but ignored during reuse

This is the largest asset bug.

`VisualSpec` contains:

```text
mechanical_version
```

and `VisualAsset` stores it. Great.

But:

```python
ensure_visual(spec, view)
```

checks:

```python
latest_canonical(
    spec.entity_id,
    spec.asset_type,
    view
)
```

and **does not check `mechanical_version`**.

So:

```text
BORIS body R17
→ TALISMAN visual R1
```

exists.

Then gameplay evolves:

```text
BORIS body R18
```

and VisualForge gets:

```text
VisualSpec(mechanical_version="R18")
```

but returns the existing R17 visual.

That directly violates:

> image ↔ gameplay truth stay coupled.

This is P0 because it's one of your new constitution-level rules.

The lookup must include:

```text
entity_id
asset_type
view
mechanical_version
identity_version / lifecycle version where relevant
```

So:

```python
latest_canonical(
    entity_id="boris",
    asset_type="TALISMAN",
    view="HERO",
    mechanical_version="R18",
)
```

If no exact match:

```text
generate new visual evolution
```

